DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260830
DTSTAMP:20260829T165946Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-53020733796497-53020733943023@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Moments in the History of East Asian Printing brings together 
 rare books\, facsimiles\, woodblocks\, broadsheets\, illustrated books\, t
 ypewriter materials\, and other objects from the East Asia Library’s col
 lections. The exhibit explores selected episodes in the history of printin
 g across China\, Korea\, and Japan\, from Buddhist woodblock printing and 
 movable type to lithography\, popular publishing\, travel prints\, visual 
 encyclopedias\, and the Chinese typewriter. Rather than offering a complet
 e chronol\n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-08-29 09:59 PDT
LOCATION:Lathrop Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Stanford Center for Continuing Medical Education] Stanford Orthop
 aedic Trauma Symposium
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260830
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260830
DTSTAMP:20260829T165946Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-53002107624161-53002107626212@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Overview\nCommunity orthopaedic surgeons take call. They manag
 e open fractures\, periprosthetic failures\, and on-call dilemmas — ofte
 n alone\, often under pressure. This symposium is built around those cases
 .\n\nThe Stanford Orthopaedic Trauma Symposium brings together high-volume
  trauma faculty for a focused\, case-driven weekend. The format covers wha
 t matters in practice: emergency room management\, challenging fractures\,
  and the decision-making that defines good trauma care. Didactics\, debate
 s\, cas\n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://stanford.cloud-cme.com/course/c
 ourseoverview?P=0&EID=52907\nLast synced: 2026-08-29 09:59 PDT
LOCATION:The Quail Lodge
URL:https://stanford.cloud-cme.com/course/courseoverview?P=0&EID=52907
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Stanford University Libraries] Text Machines: Scarlet Thread of t
 he Digital Order (1883-2026)
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260830
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260830
DTSTAMP:20260829T165946Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-53251159287291-53251159373398@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Stanford Libraries now holds an 1883 edition of a rare book\,
  Les laboureurs: poème tiré de Jocelyn\, whose pages (text and ornamen
 ts) were entirely woven on a Jacquard loom by the firm of silk merchant Jo
 seph-Alphonse Henry. This exhibition explores the cultural contexts and ma
 terial conditions of Les laboureurs’ production\, and considers parall
 els between technology-driven global change in the late nineteenth century
  and in our current day. The exhibition includes microscope images reveali
 ng the\n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-08-29 09:59 PDT
LOCATION:Green Library\, Bing Wing
END:VEVENT
